  "metaTitle": "Thornton Product Liability Attorney",
  "metaDescription": "For all product liability cases, trust the team at Dormer Harpring, LLC to get you the compensation you deserve. Call (303) 747-4404 today.",
  "body": [
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6ch",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6cg",
          "text": "Getting injured by a defective product may entitle you to financial compensation from the item’s manufacturer or distributor. The Thornton product liability lawyers at Dormer Harpring can help you with this type of lawsuit. We will guide you and your family through the legal process from the inception of your case to its completion. Our lawyers will answer all of your questions and make sure you have everything you need during this difficult time. We are committed and reputable product liability lawyers in Colorado.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6cj",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6ci",
          "text": "What Is a Product Liability Claim?",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6cm",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6ck",
          "text": "A product liability claim is a civil lawsuit that allows you to seek damages, or financial compensation, from a product manufacturer, distributor or retailer for injuries caused by a defective product. If a faulty or hazardous product injured you or a loved one, you may be eligible for monetary damages for your past and future related losses from the company that created or sold the item.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6co",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6cn",
          "text": "Types of Product Defects",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6cr",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6cp",
          "text": "Colorado product liability laws typically do not require injured consumers to prove negligence. To make things more just for the little people when going up against powerful corporations, Colorado uses a strict product liability law. This law states that if it is proven that the item contained a defect and caused the victim’s injuries, the victim does not have to prove negligence. The three types of product defects are:",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6ct",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6cs",
          "text": "Design flaw. A safety problem with how the product is inherently imagined or designed.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "number",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6cv",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6cu",
          "text": "Manufacturing error. A dangerous mistake made during the product’s manufacturing process.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "number",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6cx",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6cw",
          "text": "Marketing lapse. A safety concern with how the item is advertised, packaged or marketed.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "number",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6d0",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "s6cy",
          "text": "If your product liability case involves one of these three defects, you most likely will not have to establish negligence to receive financial compensation. Otherwise, you or your lawyer may need to base your case on the doctrine of breach of warranty or breach of duty. Our attorneys at Dormer Harpring can carefully evaluate your case to determine your legal options.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "b6d2",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
